# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unity (Base)
# Get latest template: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Unity.gitignore
# Tailored for VR projects to reduce repo size
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

.utmp/
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
*.log

# Blender autosaves
*.blend1
*.blend1.meta

# Memory/Recording captures (can be large, might include sensitive data)
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
/[Rr]ecordings/

# JetBrains Rider
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*
*.DotSettings.user
.idea/

# Visual Studio / VSCode
.vs/
.vscode/

# Gradle cache
.gradle/

# Solution / project files generated by Unity
ExportedObj/
.consulo/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Unity generated meta files for dbs
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta

# Crash info
sysinfo.txt
mono_crash.*

# Build artifacts
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.unitypackage.meta
*.app

# Crashlytics
crashlytics-build.properties

# TestRunner generated scenes
InitTestScene*.unity*

# Addressables default ignores
/ServerData
/[Aa]ssets/StreamingAssets/aa*
/[Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/link.xml*
/[Aa]ssets/Addressables_Temp*
/[Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/*/*.bin*

# Visual Scripting auto-generated
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Flow/UnitOptions.db
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Flow/UnitOptions.db.meta
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Core/Property Providers
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Core/Property Providers.meta

# Auto-generated scenes by play mode tests
/[Aa]ssets/[Ii]nit[Tt]est[Ss]cene*.unity*

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VR/Size-focused additions
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) Keep only UPM manifest files; ignore the rest of Packages to avoid massive check-ins.
#    If you embed local packages under Packages/, comment these out or whitelist those dirs.
Packages/*
!Packages/manifest.json
!Packages/packages-lock.json

# 2) IL2CPP / Bee / Player build artifacts (can be big; all regenerated)
#    Bee/Artifacts appear for newer Unity versions.
/[Bb]ee/
/[Aa]rtifacts/
/[Ii]l2cppBuildCache/

# 3) Optional: ignore baked lighting & probe data (very large, can be rebaked).
#    If your team wants to version baked data, comment these out.
# Baked GI
/[Aa]ssets/**/[Ll]ightmapSnapshot*.*
/[Aa]ssets/**/[Ll]ightmaps*/**
/[Aa]ssets/**/LightingData.asset
# Reflection probes & skyboxes generated content
/[Aa]ssets/**/ReflectionProbe-*.exr
/[Aa]ssets/**/ReflectionProbe-*.hdr
# Occlusion data
/[Aa]ssets/**/OcclusionCullingData.asset

# 4) Platform SDK intermediates commonly re-generated (esp. Android VR)
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Android/.gradle/
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Android/local.properties
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Android/.idea/
# Xcode export folders
/DerivedData/
*.xcworkspace
*.xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/

# 5) Shader caches (rebuildable)
/[Aa]ssets/**/ShaderCache/
ShaderCache/

# 6) Unity Collaborate & Plastic SCM leftovers (if you touched them before git)
.collabignore
/.plastic/
plastic.workspace

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ProjectSettings: keep deterministic settings, ignore user/machine-local stuff
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These two are user/machine-specific and noisy
ProjectSettings/EditorUserSettings.asset
ProjectSettings/Layouts.dwlt

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Common OS cruft
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# macOS / Windows
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.AppleDB
.apdisk
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL: Git LFS suggestions for VR (comment out if not using LFS).
# These file types are huge and binary; storing them via LFS keeps repo lean.
